map.json
--------
Topology (region ids, display names, adjacency) is hand-authored from public
administrative boundaries and is released under CC0 1.0.

map.svg
-------
Source:    https://simplemaps.com/static/svg/country/cz/admin1/cz.svg
           (download link on https://simplemaps.com/svg/country/cz)
Author:    Pareto Software, LLC DBA Simplemaps.com, as named in the file's
           own header comment.
Licence:   Simplemaps free SVG map licence (a custom licence; no SPDX
           identifier — Simplemaps does not use a catalogued licence).
Statement: The downloaded file's own header comment reads: "Free for
           Commercial Use, full terms at
           https://simplemaps.com/resources/svg-license. Attribution is
           appreciated!" That terms page states: "You are free to use our
           SVG maps, without any restrictions in web sites, web templates
           and software programs of any kind that you intend to sell or
           distribute. Backlinks are not required, but are highly
           appreciated." and "You are free to use our SVG maps for personal
           or commercial use."
Attribution: Appreciated but explicitly not required ("Backlinks are not
           required, but are highly appreciated"), so no footer credit was
           added to the game screen for this file.
Retrieved: 2026-08-20
Changes:   Dropped the source's "points" and "label_points" groups (city
           marker dots and label-placement circles — not part of the region
           topology) and the non-standard "name" attribute the source put on
           each region <path>. Normalized the remaining 14-path document
           with svgo (see frontend/svgo.config.mjs) — group transforms
           flattened into path data, metadata and styling stripped. Renamed
           path ids from the source's ISO 3166-2:CZ numeric codes without a
           dash (CZ10, CZ20, CZ31, ...) to this directory's map.json region
           ids (praha, stredocesky, jihocesky, ...).
